 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hey there! How's your day?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.38,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_17"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Pretty good so far.",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.98,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_29"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Is it bad to have lots of credit cards?",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 0.5,
   "block": "personal_finance.dlg11",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Not necessarily. What matters more is how much you owe on them and whether you pay on time.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.77,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "personal_finance.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I've got five. I only use two.",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 0.4,
   "block": "personal_finance.dlg11",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Having unused cards can actually help your score, because it shows available credit. But only if they don't charge annual fees.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.5,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "personal_finance.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Two of them have fees.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 1.37,
   "block": "personal_finance.dlg11",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then consider closing those. Just close one at a time, and keep your oldest card open.",
   "est_sec": 5.06,
   "gap_before": 0.61,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "personal_finance.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Why the oldest one?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 1.15,
   "block": "personal_finance.dlg11",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "The length of your credit history counts. Closing your oldest card can shorten it.",
   "est_sec": 4.44,
   "gap_before": 0.79,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "personal_finance.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Unrelated, but For Saturday's walk, do I pack lunch?",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 0.86,
   "block": "hiking.ctx11",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Depends. The route passes a mountain hut that's famous for its soup, but it closes at two. A packed lunch means you can stop anywhere. Fancy the gamble on timing?",
   "est_sec": 9.4,
   "gap_before": 1.06,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "hiking.ctx11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I was going to say the blue one, but— sorry, can I have seven seconds?",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 0.72,
   "event": "instruction",
   "kind": "think_time",
   "wait_sec": 7,
   "phrasing": "think_instruction_v2_35"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Got it.",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 0.59,
   "role": "ack",
   "phrasing": "ack_07"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "So, sandwiches in the bag, or race the clock for that soup?",
